---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import HtmlFormatter from '../../components/HtmlFormatter.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="HTML Formatter" description="Indent and format minified or messy HTML into readable markup.">
  <HtmlFormatter client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why formatted markup speeds up debugging</h2>
  <p>Minified or inconsistently indented HTML makes it hard to see the actual nesting structure — which element is inside which — slowing down debugging of layout or structural issues. Proper indentation makes the DOM hierarchy visually obvious.</p>

  <h2>How to use this tool</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Paste your minified or messy HTML.</li>
    <li>The formatted, properly indented version appears instantly.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Assuming this validates HTML.</strong> It only reformats structure — it doesn't check for unclosed tags or invalid nesting the way an HTML validator would.</li>
    <li><strong>Not reviewing deeply nested output</strong> for opportunities to simplify overly complex markup structures.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Making minified production HTML readable for debugging</li>
    <li>Cleaning up markup copied from a design tool or CMS export</li>
    <li>Reviewing the structure of a third-party HTML snippet before integrating it</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Does this fix invalid HTML?</strong> No — it reformats spacing and indentation only; structural issues (unclosed tags, invalid nesting) need to be fixed manually or with a dedicated validator.</p>
</ToolLayout>
